// Shared build settings for all targets / configurations.
//
// Local overrides (notably DEVELOPMENT_TEAM) live in Local.xcconfig, which
// is gitignored. The `#include?` directive is Xcode's "optional include":
// if Local.xcconfig is missing (e.g. on CI), the include is silently skipped.
//
// CABALMAIL_CONTROL_DOMAIN is baked into the app and macOS app entitlements
// as the `webcredentials:admin.<domain>` associated domain, which is what
// lets Password AutoFill and third-party password managers (1Password etc.)
// match the native sign-in form to the login item saved for the web app.
// The default is an RFC 2606 reserved name that can never resolve, so an
// unconfigured build still signs and merely gets no autofill match. CI
// passes the real value on the xcodebuild command line from the GitHub
// environment variable TF_VAR_CONTROL_DOMAIN (see apple.yml); a local
// build sets it in Local.xcconfig. Defaults must come BEFORE the include:
// in an xcconfig the last assignment wins, and a command-line setting beats
// both. See docs/password-autofill.md.

CABALMAIL_CONTROL_DOMAIN = cabalmail.invalid

#include? "Local.xcconfig"
